{"schemaVersion":"body.os.wger-details.v1","items":[{"id":"wger_b2ca4a136fe24c4f85b2dcb5af28d2be","wgerId":1928,"descriptionEn":"The Seated V-Grip Row is a compound pulling exercise performed on a cable machine using a close-grip \"V\" handle. While seated with your feet braced, you pull the handle toward your midsection, focusing on back thickness and mid-back development.","descriptionZh":"","author":"amaesc","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"amaesc"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"amaesc"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1928","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:36:52.056906+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_ecc4651994b84eccb5b8973e753e98a6","wgerId":1448,"descriptionEn":"Sit on bench with 60° incline Hold dumbbells beside body near the ground, palms facing outwards, arms fully extended Move dumbbells up using only biceps and without momentum","descriptionZh":"","author":"M9","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"M9"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"M9"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1448","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:52:48.594556+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_7936d8ad6a394459aa603e1e325f5e2b","wgerId":2523,"descriptionEn":"Stand facing a wall. Place your forearms vertically against the wall so your elbows and wrists are both touching it. Point your arms slightly outwards from \"straight up\". Protract your shoulders had, then slide your forearms up the wall until your elbows are about level with your chin. Slide your forearms back down the wall. Repeat as necessary.","descriptionZh":"","author":"Croak6728","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Croak6728"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Croak6728"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/2523","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-08-16T23:38:03.452046+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_ceb58be5292748c5bb2d4cc42b0a60e2","wgerId":1884,"descriptionEn":"Starting Position: Sit on the floor with both hips and knees bent at 90-degree angles. Leg Placement: Place one leg in front of you (external rotation) and the other leg out to the side/behind you (internal rotation). The shins and knees should remain flat on the ground. The Movement: Keeping your hips square, hinge your torso forward or tilt it laterally (side-to-side) toward the front leg to deepen the stretch. Target Areas: Stretches the glutes and piriformis (front leg) and the hip flexors and quads (back leg). Engages the core and obliques during lateral flexion. Goal: Improves hip mobility, specifically internal and external rotation, and relieves lower back tension.","descriptionZh":"","author":"teus_ergaster","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"teus_ergaster"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"teus_ergaster"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1884","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:56:06.520819+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_169896b290e344979d7356bee4a34697","wgerId":562,"descriptionEn":"Attach a single handle to a low cable. After selecting the correct weight, stand a couple feet back with a wide-split stance. Your arm should be extended and your shoulder forward. This will be your starting position. Perform the movement by retracting the shoulder and flexing the elbow. As you pull, supinate the wrist, turning the palm upward as you go. After a brief pause, return to the starting position.","descriptionZh":"","author":"cal.zabel","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"cal.zabel"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"cal.zabel"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/562","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:36:18.481312+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_664ddd40a595420d801f148e4bf0594c","wgerId":1081,"descriptionEn":"Starting position: Stand up with your back straight and a resistance band, towel, or broomstick handle in hand. With your hands straight in front of your body and the band between your hands, push your hands apart to both be at around 45 degrees from your body, thumbs facing down. If using a towel or broomstick handle instead, grab it with an overhand grip. Steps: Keeping your arms outstretched, rotate at the shoulders to bring your arms overhead and then down toward your glutes. Rotate at the shoulders in the opposite direction — overhead and then toward your groin. Repeat.","descriptionZh":"","author":"tinman","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"tinman"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"tinman"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1081","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:49:19.259028+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_e237611c27304d0c891bbb29d3d15297","wgerId":1714,"descriptionEn":"Lean forward to rest your hand on a chair or other object, holding a dumbbell in the other hand Gently swing the dumbbell in a circular motion","descriptionZh":"","author":"Croak6728","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Croak6728"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Croak6728"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1714","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:50:30.172182+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_b283cd479a1c40049bf5220560ef0a16","wgerId":1729,"descriptionEn":"Keep elbow fixed at your side and rotate forearm outward smoothly. Don’t let your wrist or elbow drift upward — stay in one plane.","descriptionZh":"","author":"barry","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"barry"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"barry"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1729","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:36:46.007958+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_2eead109098e4c59bdeff580a6a82748","wgerId":1715,"descriptionEn":"Lie on your side holding a dumbbell in your upper hand Tuck your elbow into your side and rest the hand in front of you Rotate the shoulder so the hand raises up Lower the hand down","descriptionZh":"","author":"Croak6728","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Croak6728"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Croak6728"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1715","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:50:31.519012+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_dadecc9463224c6693b59cb44ec79e46","wgerId":1728,"descriptionEn":"Keep your elbow tucked to your side like it's superglued there. Don’t rotate your torso — only your forearm should move.","descriptionZh":"","author":"barry","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"barry"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"barry"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1728","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:36:45.619035+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_8b0a0371c0a942a7aab768d520542fb2","wgerId":566,"descriptionEn":"Sit on a bench, the back rest should be almost vertical. Take a barbell with a shoulder wide grip and bring it up to chest height. Press the weight up, but don't stretch the arms completely. Go slowly down and repeat.","descriptionZh":"","author":"wger.de","license":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/566","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-10-18T20:00:46.724541+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_87affa4b395b437c95812bd20ea5aa7c","wgerId":567,"descriptionEn":"Sit on a bench, the back rest should be almost vertical. Take two dumbbells and bring them up to shoulder height, the palms and the elbows point during the whole exercise to the front. Press the weights up, at the highest point they come very near but don't touch. Go slowly down and repeat.","descriptionZh":"","author":"wger.de","license":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/567","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-10-10T16:54:05.623451+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_5912d7ed6a0e4b4cb30afc9f3f890fc1","wgerId":543,"descriptionEn":"","descriptionZh":"","author":"wger.de","license":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/543","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-04-15T22:23:55.116420+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_141bc87056be4749a3b9e56d5d5618b4","wgerId":569,"descriptionEn":"The exercise is basically the same as with a free barbell: Sit on a bench, the back rest should be almost vertical. Take a bar with a shoulder wide grip and bring it down to chest height. Press the weight up, but don't stretch the arms completely. Go slowly down and repeat.","descriptionZh":"","author":"wger.de","license":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/569","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:57:22.262251+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_9a644b0e86914216b2ccf058f58ec96d","wgerId":1338,"descriptionEn":"Engage the muscles Don't use momentum Controlled movement Slow movement Always keep the arms bent Don't overextend","descriptionZh":"","author":"Anastasious","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Anastasious"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Anastasious"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1338","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:51:51.240682+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_c146fa3c35a44e6e9000e12a9ee19cbd","wgerId":1443,"descriptionEn":"Stand while holding dumbbells beside body Keep arms almost fully extended Without momentum raise dumbbells to the side of your body until shoulder height, palms facing down Lower dumbbells beside body, palms facing inwards Immediately raise dumbbells in front of your body until shoulder height, palms facing down Down again This is one repetition","descriptionZh":"","author":"M9","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"M9"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"M9"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1443","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:52:45.264018+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_f956977ecc054db2a387ba6140b1ef34","wgerId":570,"descriptionEn":"The shoulder shrug (usually called simply the shrug) is an exercise in weight training used to develop the upper trapezius muscle. The lifter stands erect, hands about shoulder width apart, and raises the shoulders as high as possible, and then lowers them, while not bending the elbows, or moving the body at all. The lifter may not have as large a range of motion as in a normal shrug done for active flexibility. It is usually considered good form if the slope of the shoulders is horizontal in the elevated position.","descriptionZh":"起始位置：坐位或站位，背部挺直。 步骤： 将肩膀尽可能地向上抬起，保持 5 秒。 肩膀回到放松的位置。 重复。","author":"BFad07","license":{"id":3,"short_name":"CC0","full_name":"Creative Commons Public Domain 1.0","url":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/","author":"BFad07"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":3,"short_name":"CC0","full_name":"Creative Commons Public Domain 1.0","url":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/","author":"BFad07"},"translationLicenseZh":{"id":3,"short_name":"CC0","full_name":"Creative Commons Public Domain 1.0","url":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/","author":"BFad07"},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/570","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:57:29.170046+02:00","nameZhSource":"wger","nameZhModel":""},{"id":"wger_716286dd05b14f878b3ba0c559bcafc4","wgerId":1209,"descriptionEn":"Get into a push-up position with your shoulders directly above your hands and your feet hip-width apart. Draw your belly button in towards your spine and tighten your abdominal muscles. Lift your left foot about five centimetres off the floor. Point your toes straight down. Do not move your hips. Your body forms a straight line from your head to your heels throughout the exercise. Now bend your elbows, lower your chest to the floor and push yourself back up. Repeat the exercise on the other side.","descriptionZh":"","author":"lxmx","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"lxmx"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"lxmx"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1209","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:25:11.534687+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_7e039ac737ab49f99ae8c7efeef070cd","wgerId":1755,"descriptionEn":"on a cable rack cross the cables and pull elbows to ceiling close to the body.","descriptionZh":"","author":"","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1755","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:36:48.881598+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_43eeec70df514cad9befa35261b0caaf","wgerId":1739,"descriptionEn":"Single leg squat where one leg is behind you.","descriptionZh":"","author":"Happy","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Happy"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Happy"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1739","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-10-08T05:16:23.742689+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_6199b3c73ccb47fa89bbef7fef12c0e3","wgerId":575,"descriptionEn":"","descriptionZh":"","author":"wger.de","license":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/575","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-04-15T22:23:55.679163+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_270e108d3cd245a9807bc357317eb15c","wgerId":571,"descriptionEn":"Take a barbell and stand with a straight body, the arms are hanging freely in front of you. Lift from this position the shoulders as high as you can, but don't bend the arms during the movement. On the highest point, make a short pause of 1 or 2 seconds before returning slowly to the initial position. When training with a higher weight, make sure that you still do the whole movement!","descriptionZh":"","author":"wger.de","license":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/571","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:57:27.795399+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_72a945ec3a7f424b9a051616ef7dce91","wgerId":572,"descriptionEn":"Stand with straight body, the hands are hanging freely on the side and hold each a dumbbell. Lift from this position the shoulders as high as you can, but don't bend the arms during the movement. On the highest point, make a short pause of 1 or 2 seconds before returning slowly to the initial position. When training with a higher weight, make sure that you still do the whole movement!","descriptionZh":"","author":"wger.de","license":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"wger.de"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/572","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-10-24T15:59:16.933387+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_d36fdd3c9a354643a3fd57db78c866d6","wgerId":1188,"descriptionEn":"With a weight in one hand, extend that arm down and bend the other arm, resting your hand on your head. Now move the hand holding the weight by rotating your torso up and down.","descriptionZh":"","author":"","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1188","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-10-24T15:58:18.195917+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_919bb48a42fe4a119078ea2b5087c49f","wgerId":556,"descriptionEn":"","descriptionZh":"","author":"klabautermann","license":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"klabautermann"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"klabautermann"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/556","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-04-15T22:23:55.582184+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_2f8ee51bf49347f78b2a1da16c128f73","wgerId":576,"descriptionEn":"Hold weight in one hand. Bend side ways to the knee. Pull upo to upright position using your obliquus.","descriptionZh":"","a